+# Source and prior-attempt gate: 6200082 / AMR-061-0082
+
+The complete item is Lewis Bowen's Problem82 in Misha Kapovich, Problems on Boundaries of Groups and Kleinian Groups, printed/PDF page21, https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~kapovich/EPR/problems.pdf . The first page says most problems were collected at the AIM2005 workshop. The exact typeset item and surrounding Kleinian section were read, and page21 was visually checked. It asks whether free convex-cocompact groups in Isom(H4), including the narrower Schottky case, can have limit-set Hausdorff dimension approaching3. The ambient space is real hyperbolic four-space. No rank bound or prescribed generators appear.
+
+The pinned catalog and research record say open but provide no verified construction or proof. They are imported triage, not a substantive prior attempt and not authoritative current status. Exact ID/alias and semantic Schottky GitHub branch, commit and all-PR searches were empty; a Hausdorff/Bowen commit search was empty. Commit messages across499 locally mirrored refs were also searched. This does not claim an exhaustive content search of every historical blob or private conversation.
+
+The later primary literature supplies a negative answer. Lewis Bowen, Cheeger constants and L²-Betti numbers, Duke Mathematical Journal164(3)(2015),569–615, DOI10.1215/00127094-2871415, proves the relevant free-group uniform Cheeger gap in Corollary1.3, printed571, and the dimension consequence in Corollary1.4, printed572. Published PDF read at https://math.uchicago.edu/~shmuel/L%5E2%20cohomology%20readings/Bowen,%20Cheeger%20constants%20and%20L2-Betti%20numbers.pdf ; author's publication list https://web.ma.utexas.edu/users/lpbowen/research.html independently confirms the bibliographic data. Preprint https://arxiv.org/abs/1303.5963 began2013 and was revised2015; it is distinguished from the published version.
+
+Important proof-history qualification: the random-net continuity argument in Bowen's Theorem4.1 was incomplete. Abért–Bergeron–Biringer–Gelander, Convergence of normalized Betti numbers in nonpositive curvature, Duke Mathematical Journal172(4)(2023),633–700, DOI10.1215/00127094-2022-0029, give the replacement argument. The author version https://arxiv.org/pdf/1811.02520v3 (June2021) §2.3, pp16–18, explicitly discusses the gap and states that its Theorem2.9 applies to all Bowen applications. Its institutional record is https://real.mtak.hu/163252/ . The corrected theorem is not identical to the flawed original: it requires ball-volume bounds at every radius and an explicit nerve approximation hypothesis. CORRECTED_APPLICATION.md checks those hypotheses in the exact free-H4 application, including the boundary issue.
+
+Proposed disposition is credited already_solved0/5, subject to independent full source/proof review. This is verification of a published prior resolution and its later repaired dependency, not a new author theorem or a new proof-search turn. No numerical optimal dimension or sharp gap is claimed. Raw PDFs, page images and imported records remain local-only.
